WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.187
This query creates one contact line.

00:00:02.187 --> 00:00:05.422
The name is trimmed and has repeated whitespace normalized.

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:09.112
The email is trimmed, and NULLIF turns an empty string into NULL.

00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:10.577
The address is trimmed.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:16.452
CONCAT_WS joins the available pieces with a vertical-bar separator and skips NULL arguments.

00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:20.192
Run the query and inspect how missing values affect the output.

00:00:20.192 --> 00:00:24.642
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:24.642 --> 00:00:28.402
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:28.402 --> 00:00:32.302
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:32.302 --> 00:00:36.922
In a real setting such as a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates,

00:00:36.922 --> 00:00:41.372
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:41.372 --> 00:00:43.847
before discussing syntax.

00:00:43.847 --> 00:00:49.120
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
